{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Breathy Pipe Lead",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: a breathy, haunting pipe or pan-flute lead, the kind 80s samplers made famous: a soft tone with air around it, swelling in, a vibrato that arrives as the note holds.\n\nHow it's built: a triangle wave for the tone; white noise through a band-pass filter that follows the note (KEY) for the breath, mixed in underneath; a gentle attack. The vibrato fades in: an LFO goes through a VCA that a slow envelope opens, then into the oscillator's FM. A large Reverb.\n\nPlay: slow, expressive melodies, long notes (let the vibrato come in).\n\nTweak: the breath level (mixer 2), the attack, the vibrato envelope's ATTACK (how long before it starts), the oscillator's FM (how wide).",
